\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Paired evaluation separates selection sampling, candidate ranking and independent utility assessment. (a) Both arms select seeds using the same $W$ worlds. Ranking tolerance $\tau $ and cutoff $q$ define the restricted pool $C(\tau ,q)$. Both arms share the graph, world prefix, seed budget and tie rule. (b) A separate, shared family of $M=10,000$ evaluation worlds yields $\Delta U$, restricted minus full-reference spread. Set agreement $J$ and selection-cost ratio $\rho _T$ complete the quality--cost comparison.}}{3}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:evaluation-mechanism}{{1}{3}{Paired evaluation separates selection sampling, candidate ranking and independent utility assessment. (a) Both arms select seeds using the same $W$ worlds. Ranking tolerance $\tau $ and cutoff $q$ define the restricted pool $C(\tau ,q)$. Both arms share the graph, world prefix, seed budget and tie rule. (b) A separate, shared family of $M=10,000$ evaluation worlds yields $\Delta U$, restricted minus full-reference spread. Set agreement $J$ and selection-cost ratio $\rho _T$ complete the quality--cost comparison}{figure.1}{}}
